{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788121666,"nonce":"09ApEgHZ2/YSXVm1grMj6DPbimc=","message":"Open-question resolutions (worker, in-session on BORGES). All hook points read off the decompiled 1.6.4871 sources before writing a line; JOURNAL.md is the schema contract.\n\n**Exact hook points** — read-only Harmony postfixes on the funnels, never the UI side effects:\n\n- `letter` — `LetterStack.ReceiveLetter(Letter, string, int, bool)`, the overload every other overload converges on. `delayTicks \u003e 0` is skipped (that call only queues; `LetterStackTick` re-enters with 0 at arrival — capturing both would double-journal delayed letters), and membership in `LettersListForReading` is the arrival test (a letter `CanShowInLetterStack` rejected was dropped, not received). Per the 0.1 amendment, letter-OPEN is never used: `OpenAutomaticLetters` runs once per frame and drops bursts under fast-forward.\n- `message` — `Messages.Message(Message, bool)` funnel; `Messages.IsLive(msg)` is the landed test (`AcceptsMessage` dedupe-flashes reject the new object, so it never enters the live list).\n- `red_error` / `warning` — postfixes on `Log.Error(string)` / `Log.Warning(string)`. **Coexist with LogRelay, integrate with neither**: LogRelay owns triage (fingerprints, repeat counts, cross-session); the journal owns chronology (game-tick stamps). Neither ingests the other, so nothing is double-captured into one stream. Postfix, not prefix, so the journal records only what actually got logged.\n- `death` — `Pawn_HealthTracker.SetDead` postfix (every real death funnels there); `downed` — `Pawn_HealthTracker.MakeDowned` postfix (private, patched by name; `dinfo` bound for the damage def); `mental_break` — `MentalStateHandler.TryStartMentalState` postfix gated on `__result`. All pawns journaled with `faction` so consumers filter; a raider death mid-combat is signal, not noise.\n- `session saved` — `GameDataSaveLoader.SaveGame(string)` postfix (captures the filename; autosaves ride the same funnel). `newgame`/`loaded` — `GameComponent.StartedNewGame`/`LoadedGame` virtuals, no Harmony needed.\n- `alert_on/off` — alerts have NO notify path (verified: `AlertsReadout.CheckAddOrRemoveAlert` bare-adds/removes a private list; `Notify_Started` exists but nothing marks endings), so the scanner diffs `activeAlerts` via FieldRef on a frame cadence, labels remembered at `on` so `off` never re-reads a dead alert. Read-only: never `Recalculate`, never `GetReport`.\n\n**Alert scan cadence:** default 30 frames, configurable via `config.json` `{\"alertScanFrames\":N}` (clamped 1..600) under the protocol root. Finer than ~24 frames buys nothing — the readout itself round-robins 1/24th of all alerts per frame with 20-frame quest/precept/scenario sweeps, so the game's own detection latency dominates below that.\n\n**Warning dedupe policy:** first occurrence per exact text per session, then silent — the bench's 9 known-benign warnings cost exactly 9 journal lines per session (the amendment's requirement); repeat counting stays LogRelay's job. `red_error` is NOT deduped the same way — zero-red-errors makes each one significant — but a storm adds nothing: per-text cap of 3, then one `suppressed:true` marker event.\n\n**Job failures in v1: no.** The noise floor is enormous (every pathing hiccup and reservation clash), the player-visible layer this journal captures (messages, alerts, letters) already carries the meaningful failures, and nothing in waves 1-3 consumes a job_failed type. Revisit at 4.1 if post-mortems keep missing causes.\n\n**Session file boundary** (schema decision): one file per PROCESS session named by `sid` — the same sid status.json and every result envelope carry, so one key crosses the whole protocol; in-file `session` markers (`newgame`/`loaded`/`saved`) delimit games within a process. \n\n**journal-selftest** (scope note, not silent): the acceptance's scripted sequence (raid + letter + induced error + downed) needs a stimulus mechanism on a bench where nobody can click dev buttons, so this spec ships a `journal-selftest` verb — DevMode-gated, deliberately game-mutating, every step journaled as a `dev` event (pioneering the provenance rule 3.1 inherits). It is a minimal forerunner of the 3.1 dev layer and 3.1 supersedes it.","files":null}]}